{"name":"La Rioja","hex":"#bac00e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"La Rioja","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An autonomous community and province in northern Spain. Capital: Logroño.","A province of Argentina."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/La_Rioja"}],"entries":[{"title":"La Rioja","blocks":[{"text":"La Rioja is an autonomous community and province in Spain, in the north of the Iberian Peninsula. Its capital is Logroño. Other cities and towns in the province include Calahorra, Arnedo, Alfaro, Haro, Santo Domingo de la Calzada, and Nájera. As of 2024, it had a population of 324,184, making it the least populated autonomous community of Spain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Flag_of_La_Rioja_%28with_coat_of_arms%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_La_Rioja_%28with_coat_of_arms%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Rioja","wikidata":"Q5727"},{"title":"La Rioja (Congress of Deputies constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"La Rioja—Logroño until 1982—is one of the 52 constituencies represented in the Congress of Deputies, the lower chamber of the Spanish parliament, the Cortes Generales. The constituency currently elects four deputies. The electoral system uses the D'Hondt method and closed-list proportional voting, with a minimum threshold of three percent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/SpanishCongressDistricts%28LaRioja%29.png/330px-SpanishCongressDistricts%28LaRioja%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Rioja_(Congress_of_Deputies_constituency)","wikidata":"Q6464884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Fa%C3%A7ade_of_Santa_Mar%C3%ADa_de_la_Redonda_in_Logro%C3%B1o.jpg/250px-Fa%C3%A7ade_of_Santa_Mar%C3%ADa_de_la_Redonda_in_Logro%C3%B1o.jpg?utm_source=